    "body": "**TLDR:** Compile Muse Spark's base RMSNorm (`muse_spark_rmsnorm` region): decode -2 to -5%, training -0.1 to -1.6%, prefill ~0, for a 2-line model change.\n\n**Problem**\n1. **Residual-stream norms.** `attention_norm`, `ffn_norm`, `post_attention_norm`, `pre_expert_norm` and the final norm use `MuseSparkRMSNorm.forward`.\n2. **Eager.** After PR 1 they run ATen's fused `rms_norm` (fwd 1 kernel, bwd 2) plus a separate weight-add and cast.\n3. **Cost.** Small per call, but at decode every kernel launch counts.\n\n**Solution**\n1. **Region.** `@local_compile(\"muse_spark_rmsnorm\", batch_invariant=False, recompile_limit=16)` on `MuseSparkRMSNorm.forward`, enabled in the model config.\n2. **Graph budget.** One region serves four call shapes (fp32 stream with weight, bf16 without weight, 4096-wide expert norm, final norm) x grad mode x dynamic T: 12 graphs, so the limit is raised to 16.\n3. **Unchanged.** The norm math.\n\n**Results**\n```text\nNumerics: not bitwise: compiled reduction order differs (forward output and all grads differ)\n\n2 layers, native dims, one EP32 rank's experts, GB300, ms, in-process interleaved A/B, min of 3 rounds\n                    T                    main     PR 3  this PR   vs PR 3  vs main\ntrain fwd+bwd       2k launch           22.88    17.79    17.86     +0.4%   -21.9%\n                    2k graphs           21.54    16.89    16.87     -0.1%   -21.7%\n                    4k launch           43.40    34.22    33.70     -1.5%   -22.4%\n                    4k graphs           42.13    33.35    33.17     -0.6%   -21.3%\n                    16k launch         171.50   137.40   136.62     -0.6%   -20.3%\n                    16k graphs         171.41   138.02   135.82     -1.6%   -20.8%\nprefill (no_grad)   2k                   7.64     5.71     5.67     -0.7%   -25.9%\n                    16k                 59.31    45.18    45.17     -0.0%   -23.8%\ndecode (no_grad)    1 seqs x 1           1.07     0.96     0.92     -5.0%   -14.6%  (*)\n                    8 seqs x 1           1.10     0.96     0.93     -3.6%   -15.7%\n                    64 seqs x 1          1.33     1.16     1.12     -3.5%   -15.8%\n                    256 seqs x 1         1.55     1.23     1.20     -2.4%   -22.8%\n(*) another GPU process was present; deltas hold (interleaved).\n```\nCorrectness: not bitwise; the error vs fp64 is the same as eager's (output 5.1e-8, input grad 5.7e-8, weight grad 1.7e-3 in bf16; weight grad 1.3e-7 vs 2.2e-7 in fp32).\n2 layers at 4k: the difference from PR 3 is 0.9x what a 1-ulp change of the input causes.\nGraphs: 12 across training and inference shapes, limit 16.\nNOTE: graph count measured on text shapes; the multimodal model also calls this region on perception embeddings (`perception_emb_norm`), not counted.\n\n**Test plan**\n`pytest tests/unit_tests/gpu/models/muse_spark/test_attention_compile.py` (adds region vs eager for the norm, incl. weight grad)\n\n",
